SUMMARY:World Affairs Council of Western North Carolina: The U.S.-UK Special Relationship — An Insider’s Take
DESCRIPTION:Drawing on her 34 years as an American diplomat\, including more than a decade working directly in and on the United Kingdom\, Ambassador Barbara Stephenson explores the history and current state of the U.S.-UK Special Relationship. She will discuss the countries’ close cooperation in intelligence\, military\, and diplomatic affairs\, as well as longstanding and emerging points of tension. Through personal anecdotes and photographs from a state visit by the Obamas\, Stephenson will offer behind-the-scenes insight into this important bilateral relationship.  \nThis event will take place in the Reuter Center and is free and open to the public. \nAbout the Speaker \nBarbara Stephenson is the William and Anne Harrison Vice Provost for Global Affairs and Chief Global Officer at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. A former U.S. ambassador and career Foreign Service officer\, she served as U.S. Ambassador to Panama and was the first woman to serve as deputy ambassador and acting ambassador at the U.S. Embassy in London. She previously served as president of the American Foreign Service Association and dean of the Leadership and Management School at the Foreign Service Institute. She is also chair of the World Affairs Councils of America.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/world-affairs-council-of-western-north-carolina-the-u-s-uk-special-relationship-an-insiders-take/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Event-Calendar-TEMPLATE-20.png
END:VEVENT
